# Victrix

**Victrix** is a personal, non-commercial research project that runs the Xbox
Series X|S build of *Grand Theft Auto VI* natively on a Windows PC: the game's
own x86-64 code runs unchanged, Victrix stands in for the console's system
libraries, and the console's graphics shaders are translated for a PC graphics
card on the fly.

This page only tells you that the project exists and how far it is.
**The source code is not published** (see "Why no code here").

## What this project does not share

- **No game files, code, assets or other intellectual property** of Rockstar
  Games, Take-Two Interactive or any other game studio is included here or in
  the project. Nothing from the game is ever stored in the project's files.
- **No downloads of the game, and no help with getting it.** Anyone running
  software like this must supply **their own, legally owned copy** of the game.
- Nothing for bypassing DRM or copy protection.
- No console SDK files, keys or binaries.

Victrix is not affiliated with, endorsed by or connected to Rockstar Games,
Take-Two Interactive, Microsoft or Xbox. *Grand Theft Auto* and *Grand Theft
Auto VI* are trademarks of their owners and are named here only to say which
game the project is about.

## Status (2026-11-24)

Tested on one PC: Windows 11, AMD Ryzen 7 7800X3D, NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Ti,
32 GB DDR5.

| Part of the game | State |
|---|---|
| Boot, menus, intro video, saves | work |
| Loading into the world | works |
| Opening cutscene | plays, about 5-7 fps |
| First gameplay scene | renders and runs at about 4 fps on average |
| Lighting in shadow | missing: the game's ray-traced lighting does not run yet, so shadowed areas are black |
| Effects | some are still missing (shaders that cannot be translated yet) |
| Stability | no crash in recent runs of up to ~15 minutes |

**Not playable yet.** This is an early research build, not something to play
the game with.

## Built on the work of others

Victrix combines and builds on these open-source projects. All credit for
their work goes to their authors:

| Project | Author(s) | Licence |
|---|---|---|
| [VIctory](https://github.com/Marvisak/VIctory) | Marvisak and contributors | GPL-3.0-or-later |
| [victory-gta6](https://github.com/fxceless/victory-gta6) | fxceless and contributors | GPL-3.0 |
| [XCL](https://github.com/ivall/xcl) | ivall and contributors | GPL-2.0-only |

VIctory is the base (loader, system libraries, Direct3D 12 back end, shader
translator); victory-gta6 adds world rendering and speed work for NVIDIA cards;
XCL's shader recompiler is used as a fallback for shaders the others cannot
translate yet. Victrix's own additions so far are texture-streaming and
frame-pacing fixes measured on the PC above (about 1.2 fps to about 4 fps in the
first gameplay scene).

If you want to run or contribute to this kind of work, the projects above are
public and are the right place to start.

## Why no code here

Victrix combines code under GPL-3.0 (VIctory, victory-gta6) with code under
GPL-2.0-only (XCL). Those two licences do not allow the combined code to be
published, so it stays private and is used for personal research only. Any
improvement that can be shared under its project's own licence is best offered
to that project directly.

